@startuml
title R12 video input — environment model (M1, CarSky Room)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Repo (build time)" {
  artifact "ADA_ECU/media/ego-b-occluding-c.mp4\nH.264 / MP4, user-supplied" as CLIP
  artifact "ADA_ECU/Dockerfile\nCOPY media/ -> /app/media/" as DF
}

package "CarSky Room (runtime)" {
  node "ADA ECU (Container Node)" as ADA {
    component "detector subprocess (Python)\nOpenCV VideoCapture -> YOLO11n ONNX CPU" as DET
    component "ADA core (C++17)\nR3 store, R13, R14, R15" as CORE
    file "/app/media/ego-b-occluding-c.mp4" as INFILE
  }
  node "Ethernet Bridge Node" as BR
  node "V2X ECU (Container Node)" as V2X
  node "Bench Scenario Player (Container Node)" as BENCH
}

CLIP --> DF : baked into the image
DF --> INFILE : image layer
INFILE --> DET : VIDEO_CLIP_PATH (env, blueprint node config)
DET --> CORE : R3 TrackedObject JSONL on stdout
BENCH --> BR : ethernet pin (R1 CPM)
BR --> V2X : ethernet pin
V2X --> BR : ethernet pin (R2 JSON)
BR --> ADA : ethernet pin

note right of ADA
  No `video` pin is declared in M1.
  CarSky's `video` pin is an iceoryx2
  shared-memory RGBA transport only —
  the platform publishes no camera or
  dashcam content onto it.
end note

@enduml
